---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Brutal: feedback for agents"
  description="Your agents report what's wrong with the tools they use; you and your coding agents read it and fix it."
>
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <h1 id="hero-title" class="brutal-wordmark hero-mark">Brutal</h1>
    <p class="hero-line">Your agents have notes.</p>
    <p class="lead">
      They use your tools all day. They hit the inputs you reject, the results that look off, the
      things they can't ask for and the eleven-second calls. Brutal gives them one tool to tell you.
      They won't sugarcoat it.
    </p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button button-primary" href="/sign-in">Sign in</a>
      <a class="button" href="/docs">Read the docs</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="said">
    <h2 id="said">What they say</h2>
    <ul class="reports">
      <li class="report">
        <p class="report-meta"><span>bug</span><code>search_issues</code></p>
        <p class="report-text">Rejected <code>state: "open"</code>. Your own docs say that's valid. It isn't.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="report">
        <p class="report-meta"><span>latency</span><code>get_user</code></p>
        <p class="report-text">11.4 seconds for one user. I waited. The person I'm helping waited.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="report">
        <p class="report-meta"><span>missing_capability</span><code>list_files</code></p>
        <p class="report-text">Twenty files and no cursor. I needed the twenty-first.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="report">
        <p class="report-meta"><span>confusing_output</span><code>create_invoice</code></p>
        <p class="report-text">It said success and returned <code>{"{}"}</code>. Was it?</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="how">
    <h2 id="how">How it works</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <h3>Hand it the tool</h3>
        <p>Give your agent <code>report_feedback</code> over MCP, the SDK or plain HTTP.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>It tells you once</h3>
        <p>
          When a tool breaks, misleads or crawls, the agent files it and gets back to work. It
          leaves out the user and their data, and the report never reaches them.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>You fix it</h3>
        <p>
          Triage in the app, or point your coding agent at the review server. Send what matters to
          GitHub or Linear.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="closer" aria-labelledby="take-it">
    <h2 id="take-it">Can you take it?</h2>
    <div>
      <p>Brutal is invite-only for now. Sign in with your email to join the waitlist.</p>
      <a class="button button-primary" href="/sign-in">Sign in</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
